 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "How the falling leaves fall on our\nCurved fence - how they are fallen away\nIn small clusters, scattered\nAbove and below it array.\nWhat gives them their coldness? Where ever\nWe stand in any shade of decay,\nThey cling to the branches above,\nAnd touch the ground below us away.\nWhat do they fear from us? Our\nMotion that draws from away,\nFalling down again, again,\nTo their natural place array.",
